# Probe output never belongs in the repo. A dump of a third party's page carries
# whatever they ship to visitors: rivieracinemas.fi's Maps JS key ended up in
# probe/rv-films.html and tripped GitHub secret scanning (alert #1, commit 626b865).
# Probe a target, read the answer, write the finding into IDEAS.md, commit nothing raw.
probe/
probe-*.txt
probe-*.html

# Local scratch
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
# Written into every worktree by the agent tooling, not by this project. Untracked it
# shows up as a pending change in all ten of them and gets offered as a pull request;
# tracked it would be a public file this repo does not author and cannot keep accurate.
AGENTS.md

# Atomic-write staging files (common.write_json), in case a run dies between write and replace
*.tmp

# Conditional-GET validator cache (common.fetch cache=True). Never committed: it holds
# verbatim copies of third parties' pages, which is exactly what the probe/ rule above
# exists to keep out of a public repo. Restored between Actions runs by actions/cache.
.http-cache/
